; type-algebra shorthand exemplar — a schema for a decision ledger, written
; as UDON. Dialect reading (proposed, not ratified): element suffixes are
; arities (! = {1,1}, ? = {0,1}, * = {0,*}, + = {1,*}); a leading {n,m} tail
; is the general arity; [key!] declares keyed-and-required; .open / .closed
; is the row tail (P1: extraction may emit .open only; .closed is a fiat act
; and carries its reason). A trailing ! on an attribute KEY is dialect-
; assigned (core reads it as an ordinary key named "date!"). ? on a key is
; core flag semantics TODAY — measured: ":confidence? float" snaps the flag
; true, re-owns "float" as CONTENT, ends the attribute phase, and every
; later attribute draws AttributeAfterChildren. Whether the schema dialect
; spells optionality with ?, or unmarked-optional as this exemplar elects,
; or core's flag/re-own rule itself moves, is an OPEN election (zero
; consumers of ? semantics exist — see README N6). Here: unmarked keys are
; optional {0,1}; ! is required {1,1}; stacks carry {n,m} on the value.
; Recognition story per the RULED 0.9.1 text (CORE 5.3/5.4/6.2/6.5), which
; is this spike's only oracle; a run through the 0.8-lineage parser served
; as a typo-check only (that artifact is known non-conformant to the
; current spec and validates nothing here).

|schema[decision-record] :version 0.1 :status proposed
  A |decision is the ledger's record grain. Prose inside a schema is
  documentation; the dialect types it TEXT and otherwise ignores it.

  |decision+[key!].open
    :date! <temporal>
    :by! str
    :status! str
    :confidence float
    :supersedes str{0,2}
    |reason!
    |impact?
    |ref{0,7}
